    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the disposable-domain blocklist rejection for owner creation/update, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (the existing `Reject*` step + checked exception + escalation handler pattern).\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java` \u2014 reads the normalized `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, extracts the email domain, and throws when it's in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Skips `null`/blank emails (already normalized away by the preceding step).\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 checked exception.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainHandler.java` \u2014 responds **400 Bad Request**.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires exception \u2192 handler.\n\n**Wiring changes:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` \u2014 inserted the `rejectDisposableEmailDomain` step immediately after `normalizeEmail` (so the address is already validated and lower-cased before the domain check; the PUT step carries the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbors).\n\nThe check runs after normalization, so it's case-insensitive and matches on the exact domain label. The new acceptance test (`x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes, and the full suite is green.",
